+// Stealth Chromium: WebGPU adapter persona (spec patches/16-webgpu-fingerprint.md).
+//
+// Identity-seed-driven GPUAdapter spoofing. While fingerprinting is active
+// the adapter reports the persona vendor/architecture/device (Apple on the
+// macOS persona, an NVIDIA model from the embedded database otherwise), the
+// advertised feature set is filtered through a plausibility allowlist, and
+// the advertised limits are clamped to the persona table below. Without
+// --fingerprint every getter reports "no spoof" and callers keep the real
+// adapter values (feature filtering is the one unconditional piece, matching
+// the vendor build).
+//
+// The NVIDIA model selection mirrors modules/webgl/gpu_fingerprint.cc
+// (patch 0016): same database order, same seed salt ("gpu_renderer"), same
+// first-match substring lookup for --fingerprint-gpu-renderer. The two
+// tables MUST stay in sync so WebGL UNMASKED_RENDERER_WEBGL and the WebGPU
+// adapter info can never disagree for a given identity.
+
